{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/284076-alternative-lunar-exaltation-methods-lunars-and-the-call","id":284076,"title":"Alternative Lunar Exaltation methods: Lunars and the call.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-16T13:03:25-07:00","id":284076,"title":"Alternative Lunar Exaltation methods: Lunars and the call.","content":"I was talking in another thread about alternate Exaltation 'narratives' for Lunars and how they could be made more distinct; and I had an idea that I thought was worth its own post.<br /> <br /> Basically, none of the current Exalted really explore the idea of the &quot;hero's journey&quot; or a &quot;call to adventure.&quot; Solars are self-made, but their Exaltation is a sudden unexpected moment of transcendence; Abyssals and Infernals have to agree to Exalt, but it's one moment where they're made an offer, not a traditional call to adventure. Sidereals are called by fate, but lack any choice and therefore aren't really self-made.<br /> <br /> For references, I'm thinking of something like Luke Skywalker leaving behind his life (and, eventually, getting called to Degobah), or Bran Stark getting called beyond the wall by the Three-Eyed Crow, or Monkey choosing to leap through the waterfall to become the Monkey King, or the basic concept of the Campbellian Hero's Journey. Potential Lunars see or are touched by a call to go on some journey that goes beyond the bounds of their normal life; and those who follow this path Exalt somewhere along the way. Those who fail or who reject the call (or people who are still on their journey) remain mortal, but are perhaps touched in small subtle ways -- they might be able to talk to specific types of animals, say.<br /> <br /> The journey would typically begin with a prophetic dream or some other portent, often some form of visitation by Luna or one of her agents (including, sometimes, other Lunars.) Existing Lunars are frequently involved in the journey on some level -- sometimes as companions; sometimes an elder Lunar is your destination, someone to bring out and train you in your potential powers. These Lunars are themselves alerted to you by dreams and portents, naturally -- an elder Lunar will receive a vision from Luna of a promising student, or another young Lunar will receive a vision of a potential new companion who needs to be protected on their journey. Lunars who desire students or companions (and perhaps who pray to Luna for them) will occasionally be answered by visions guiding them to a new Lunar candidate so they can serve these roles.<br /> <br /> The journey generally takes you outside of the world you know. Frequently this means into the Wyld, but it can also mean simply the wilderness, or into older and darker areas of a city, or into stranger places like the Underworld or Hell.<br /> <br /> The call sometimes involves a specific quest; but sometimes it's just a journey (although rarely an entirely easy or straightforward journey.) Often, along the way, the Lunar will continue to have strange dreams or see portents of their possible futures and Luna's plans for them.<br /> <br /> At the end of the journey, the Lunar generally faces a choice: They can come back to civilization, bringing the powers and secrets they have wrested from the outer world; or they can remain on the periphery fighting to protect the world from without. Either option is valid, of course (and Lunars aren't irrevocably committing themselves to one path or the other), but how they thought about that choice -- what they decided and why -- would help define them in a uniquely Lunar fashion.<br /> <br /> (Obviously most Lunars, until recently, have been somewhat pushed towards &quot;remain on the periphery&quot;, since returning to civilization as a Lunar carries significant risks; but both options remain available.)<br /> <br /> <br /> I think that this does several neat things for Lunars. First, it's a way to give them a role of &quot;rangers&quot; -- people who walk outside the world -- without completely tying them to barbarian stereotypes. You can approach it in many ways, and even if you want to do the barbarian thing, the idea of Lunar Exaltation as a vision that calls you on a journey gives you a way to have your character be a Dances-With-Wolves type who was pulled outside of their life into the periphery -- it opens up a lot more options for uniquely Lunar stories.<br /> <br /> Second, by incorporating other Lunars into your journey, this provides a way for Lunars to have a coherent identity as a group. Not <i>every</i> Lunar has companions or an instructor, but this provides a straightforward way to insert those things, which can be a uniquely Lunar part of your backstory -- any Lunars who helped you on your journey or instructed you at the end are potential allies and friends (assuming they're not already other PCs, of course.)<br /> <br /> Third, it fits into the Lunar's themes as shamans and spiritualists while still leaving a lot of flexibility in terms of what the journey looks like and how it feels -- it doesn't tie you to one thing; it can be interpreted as a test from Luna to prove you're worthy of a Lunar Exaltation instead.<br /> <br /> Fourth, partially because of that, it feels fairly uniquely Lunar; none of the other Exalted work this way, and it's hard to picture how they could. It ties a lot of disparate Lunar themes (and oddities about them) together around a central narrative, without being too confining -- the vast majority of existing Lunar concepts, I think, could work with this. (Especially since it's possible for the journey to be as simple as &quot;walk over there and step into that ominous grove&quot; -- sometimes just the willingness to do it and to step into the unknown is what's important.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 10-16-2014, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T13:10:52-07:00","id":284102,"title":"","content":"At what point do they actually have an Exaltation and magic powers? When they choose to start the quest? Or at the end? I might say &quot;when they commit to undertaking the quest&quot; is when they are granted their powers, but with the caveat that whatever subconscious acceptance means they cannot turn from the path of that journey until it ends, one way or another. So they gain the miracle and the instincts of using it at the start, with the caveat that hey have locked themselves into a quest or journey that really cannot be avoided or deferred; it's part of the Exaltation affecting the world itself.<br /> <br /> All in all your idea reminds me of the adulthood initiation rights of the Orlanthi in the Glorantha setting (HeroQuest), when pretty much all young Orlanthi men journey to the Other Side, into the Godtime, to Heroquest as Heort and participate in the battle of I Fought, We Won. Succeed and you're an adult (and there are multiple times while you live the myth that you can succeed and end or just keep going and see how far you get, with greater peril and greater reward the farther you go); fail and you either die on the Other Side or make it back but are outcast from society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T13:22:22-07:00","id":284133,"title":"","content":"Initially, my thought was that they Exalt at the end of their quest, but it could vary; some might Exalt at the climax, when they most need their powers, while others might suddenly find they have them when they reach for them, somewhere along the way -- you're trying to fit through this tangled briar, and suddenly you've slipped through easily, and you realize it's because you're a fox.<br /> <br /> Exalting at the beginning would lose some of the mythological heft, I think -- you're (thematically) going on a journey outside the world in order to wrest power and wisdom from it, whether that's into the Wyld or just into the huge ominous forest out back. So you have to actually go there and do things before your powers appear.<br /> <br /> Although it might be appropriate for you to develop some minor powers (like the ability to speak to a specific type of animal) at the beginning, marking you as 'special' in that way; these things would probably have to be subsets of intro-tier Lunar charms or of powers all Lunars get if they're going to be expressed mechanically (because otherwise what happened to them when you became a Lunar?) Or perhaps they could be odd powers you can purchase as merits, since they're in theory available to mortals... the Lunar Exaltation could sometimes be attracted to people who already have a bit of the &quot;outside&quot; in them and therefore already have some strange powers like that. People touched by the Wyld, people with distant divine or Exalted ancestors... I imagine there are lots of mortals in Creation with strange inexplicable subtle powers for one reason or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 10-16-2014, 04:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T13:26:09-07:00","id":284137,"title":"","content":"I kind of like an idea of gradual power but I dunno if it would work. Like as the journey starts, you discover the power to shapeshift. You can cycle through several forms of animals local to the region you are in, and your human form, to overcome obstacles on your journey, settling in to your Spirit Shape by the end. Gaining the full power of Charms at the climax, or when most needed as an instinctive response to mortal danger, is also pretty cool and evocative of what Lunars want to do I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T13:50:16-07:00","id":284154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/284076-alternative-lunar-exaltation-methods-lunars-and-the-call#post284076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The journey generally takes you outside of the world you know. Frequently this means into the Wyld, but it can also mean simply the wilderness, or into older and darker areas of a city, or into stranger places like the Underworld or Hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though what you're going for would be best conveyed by a sense of leaving a comfortable context or perspective, rather than actual other world. That can include where Conan starts living in cities and is rather bewildered.<br /> <br /> I'm getting a sense of the origin journey of Bruce Wayne in Batman Begins from this. It's interesting.<br /> <br /> Personally, I've been starting to develop my own idea, based on some Flat Earth stuff, of Lunars coming from situations where they flaunted or defied some serious local taboo or tradition. Like a mythic version of that one kid who climbs the huge tree or goes into the ruined house that everybody else says is too dangerous. Maybe in particular the people who did that, suffered for it, but kept struggling in defiance or remained unbowed and enthusiastic anyway.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T15:53:43-07:00","id":284304,"title":"","content":"Cool ideas. It also offers a reason for why and how Lunars can find new Lunars before the Sidereals and Whld Hunt on a consistent basis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T16:22:42-07:00","id":284315,"title":"","content":"I think the idea of a more 'gradual' Exaltation, rather than a single perfect moment of realization, might suit Lunars. Lunars are ever-changing, enduring and adaptable. It makes sense that they'd be Chosen from among people who are willing to leave their familiar comfort zone, literally or metaphorically, confront the unknown and change - themselves or the world around them. So that's indeed an intriguing idea put forward here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T16:28:03-07:00","id":284337,"title":"","content":"I actually really like this. It's evocative of Lunars as world-walkers, and gives them something no other Exalted really have. One amusing possiblity that occurred to me was someone from a barbarian culture having his journey &quot;outside the world&quot; take him into a large city like Nexus, or even the Blessed Isle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T17:36:46-07:00","id":284374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/284076-alternative-lunar-exaltation-methods-lunars-and-the-call?p=284337#post284337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually really like this. It's evocative of Lunars as world-walkers, and gives them something no other Exalted really have. One amusing possiblity that occurred to me was someone from a barbarian culture having his journey &amp;quot;outside the world&amp;quot; take him into a large city like Nexus, or even the Blessed Isle.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's certainly better than the current one, which doesn't do anything the Zenithoid's don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T18:01:57-07:00","id":284416,"title":"","content":"I would suggest not giving them the Exaltation when they begin the journey, or when they end it, but when they need it, or when they realize that it is not just a calling of a journey or an adventure, but the calling of a new life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T18:03:23-07:00","id":284418,"title":"","content":"Also, thinking about the people who rejected or turned back from the journey without Exalting (Moon-touched?), I think I'd say that from Luna's perspective you never fail for good -- once you are a candidate, you're always a candidate on some level, and the wilds might call you again to receive a Lunar Exaltation at a later date. This would make them more interesting for Lunars to interact with than just turning them into failed Lunars (and would also have more potential for stories where people are playing them.) If Lunars can identify these people, it also means that a Lunar might have them as lieutenants or companions (or just contacts within civilization, for Lunars on the periphery) -- people who have not <i>yet</i> made the journey, or who turned back when called, but who might do it in the future if the time is right.<br /> <br /> So, for example, your Lunar might be a ranger who wanders the wilds near a city, protecting it from rising Fair Folk incursions, while relying on a moon-touched shopkeeper who has felt Luna's call but has not yet yielded to it as a contact who keeps you informed about what's going on within its walls.<br /> <br /> (Assuming there is still a finite number of discrete Lunar Exaltations, that would mean that they're basically a shortlist of people who might feel the call again when another Lunar Exaltation is available. This also makes them a bit more distinct from Abyssals and Infernals, for whom a 'no' is final -- very final, for an Abyssal. The idea of having potential Exalts around overlaps with DBs and Sidereals to an extent, but I think it's fairly distinct -- you can't deliberately produce them, and these people would be much lower in number than DB offspring. And unlike Sidereals, they're not <i>fated</i> to Exalt; they just feel the call and may or may not one day answer it.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 10-16-2014, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T19:08:21-07:00","id":284504,"title":"","content":"Also a cool idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T19:40:08-07:00","id":284517,"title":"","content":"Giving second chances, and making both Exaltation itself and the end of the quest indefinite, seems a very Luna-esque approach to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T20:27:28-07:00","id":284555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/284076-alternative-lunar-exaltation-methods-lunars-and-the-call?p=284517#post284517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Giving second chances, and making both Exaltation itself and the end of the quest indefinite, seems a very Luna-esque approach to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, it also adds a twist to it that the Immaculate Faith would just LOVE to interpret in a way that lends the anathema theory legitimacy.<br /> <br /> The essence of the silver anathema preys upon mortals it can entice to journey beyond their rightful place in the world, succoring them with promises of discovery and adventure and claiming those who trust it's honeyed words.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T20:32:26-07:00","id":284560,"title":"","content":"God I wish this were canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T20:33:16-07:00","id":284561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/284076-alternative-lunar-exaltation-methods-lunars-and-the-call?p=284560#post284560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">God I wish this were canon.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Keep your fingers crossed Omicron. Just maybe we'll see a character who has to work for years to earn his Exaltation, because sometimes Luna works that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T20:49:55-07:00","id":284581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PlotVitalNPC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/284076-alternative-lunar-exaltation-methods-lunars-and-the-call?p=284555#post284555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed, it also adds a twist to it that the <b>Immaculate Faith</b> would just LOVE to interpret in a way that lends the anathema theory legitimacy.<br /> <br /> The essence of the silver anathema preys upon mortals it can entice to journey beyond their rightful place in the world, succoring them with promises of discovery and adventure and claiming those who trust it's honeyed words.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidenote: Immaculate Philosophy, encompassing the Realm, the Immaculate faith of Lookshy, and any other groups of Immaculates as an umbrella term. Immaculate faith, as noted, specifically refers to the more Shogunate-like religion of the Seventh Legion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T20:57:55-07:00","id":284585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/284076-alternative-lunar-exaltation-methods-lunars-and-the-call?p=284581#post284581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sidenote: Immaculate Philosophy, encompassing the Realm, the Immaculate faith of Lookshy, and any other groups of Immaculates as an umbrella term. Immaculate faith, as noted, specifically refers to the more Shogunate-like religion of the Seventh Legion.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they want to be referred to properly, they should use more than one word of difference to distinguish themselves <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Nobody refers to Abrahamic religion as a whole as 'Judaism', 'Christianity', or 'Islam'.<br /> <br /> From now on I shall call them the Immaculate Confusion.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T21:06:49-07:00","id":284589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/284076-alternative-lunar-exaltation-methods-lunars-and-the-call?p=284560#post284560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">God I wish this were canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah barring some amazing 3e change in this aspect of Lunars (that I will not hold my breath for), I'm going to use this in my games from now on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T00:36:04-07:00","id":284733,"title":"","content":"The Lunar Exaltation itself stalks its candidate as they go through their trials. It waits until the perfect moment to pounce and Exalt them!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T03:24:07-07:00","id":284805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PlotVitalNPC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/284076-alternative-lunar-exaltation-methods-lunars-and-the-call?p=284585#post284585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If they want to be referred to properly, they should use more than one word of difference to distinguish themselves <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Nobody refers to Abrahamic religion as a whole as 'Judaism', 'Christianity', or 'Islam'.<br /> <br /> From now on I shall call them the Immaculate Confusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, there's some hefty differences between various Christian factions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anywho, I like this.<br /> <br /> I think that how it should work is that there is in fact no one moment of Exaltation; Exaltations-as-shards didn't add that much to the game-line. So instead, it is *completely* a gradual process; they take in the essence of Luna as they go through their quest, and can use it, but if they turn back before the end, it will fade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T03:46:31-07:00","id":284810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/284076-alternative-lunar-exaltation-methods-lunars-and-the-call?p=284560#post284560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">God I wish this were canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>3e Lunars are still a ways out, so... fingers crossed? Not saying the developers will poach ideas from this thread, mind you, but maybe what they have in mind is not dissimilar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T04:23:19-07:00","id":284819,"title":"","content":"I don't like this idea. It implies that Lunars' powers won't be connected, in any way, to the lives they were living before- and if your Lunar's character arc is motivated at all by their time as a mortal, that discrepancy won't be a good thing.<br /> For example, I consider Seven Devils Clever one of the few good Lunars, writing-wise. And what defined her was that she was a stubborn kid who would not stand by and watch people suffer while she could do something about it. Not the jaunt into the rainforest she took because some glowing stranger told her to. Was it wise of the writers to define <i>all </i>Lunars as territory guards? No, but to define them as the exact opposite runs into the same problem.<br /> Not all Lunar characters are going to have the time or the inclination to go on a vision quest, even if they have a solid reason to- and every single Lunar who is not a mystic or wanderer will want a solid reason to. And given that we're trying to move away from 'Silver Solars', where does that leave the proto-Lunars who do?<br /> <br /> Also, obligatory <i>Heralds of Valdemar</i> reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T07:02:04-07:00","id":284924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/284076-alternative-lunar-exaltation-methods-lunars-and-the-call?p=284819#post284819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It implies that Lunars' powers won't be connected, in any way, to the lives they were living before</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it doesn't. I take all of this as...you have to be a certain kind of person, pursuing your goals without much success and having exhausted many avenues but <i>still trying, no matter how desperate the attempt is,</i> to move them forward...then the world itself shifts to show you an avenue you were incapable of seeing before.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/284076-alternative-lunar-exaltation-methods-lunars-and-the-call?p=284819#post284819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what defined her was that she was a stubborn kid who would not stand by and watch people suffer while she could do something about it. Not the jaunt into the rainforest she took because some glowing stranger told her to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does not want to stand by and watch people suffer --&gt; sees signs and portents and dreams to find a way to help people --&gt; journey thing inside the city she lives in --&gt; Exalt.<br /> <br /> Nobody is saying that an urban pro-Lunar in Port Calin is going to have to run off into the southeastern jungle to Exalt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 10-17-2014, 10:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T09:30:19-07:00","id":285020,"title":"","content":"I'm not too big on choice as an element of Exaltation. <br /> <br /> Particularly not a long term choice - it's there in all the Exaltations, everyone's Exaltation is triggered by a choice, but it's not sustained or long term, not necessarily thought out and planned and known, more like a person seizing a power or following an intuition. I think you get more interesting stories when Exaltation's like that.<br /> <br /> I think another part of what I find here is that I actually don't think different circumstances of Exaltation mean that much, as they're already done with when we enter play. Really I wonder why this element makes sense as coming before the Exaltation, rather than following the Exaltation? For all that Lunars do canonically go through trials, hunts and journeys after Exaltation, and it would make sense for that to be more a part of Lunar Exaltation itself and not only Lunar culture alone. That post Exaltation situation is what would probably most meaningfully set the Lunars apart, not a difference in whether the god chooses you for your strong, unique qualities (preferably not just reduced to the capacity for survival, I guess) and grants you power in a sudden rush, like with Strawmaiden Janest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T11:27:09-07:00","id":285166,"title":"","content":"I could see a lot of cool in this. ^_^ It'd certainly make me happy. I'm curious what form the EX3 Lunar Exaltation <i>will </i>wind up taking. It might just remain, &quot;basically the same as a Solar Exaltation, though Luna appears in person to bear witness in a way the Sun does not,&quot; but we'll see; here's hoping for something more distinct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/284076-alternative-lunar-exaltation-methods-lunars-and-the-call?p=285020#post285020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not too big on choice as an element of Exaltation.<br /> <br /> Particularly not a long term choice - it's there in all the Exaltations, everyone's Exaltation is triggered by a choice, but it's not sustained or long term, not necessarily thought out and planned and known, more like a person seizing a power or following an intuition. I think you get more interesting stories when Exaltation's like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an oversimplification. Different Exaltations work differently. Dragonblooded Exaltation isn't a choice, it's an inheritance. Liminal Exaltation is definitely not a choice: the new Liminal is a person who simply didn't exist before; it technically isn't even the choice of whomever accidentally created one. Alchemical Exaltation is a kind of choice, as you've framed it, but it is of necessity one that is sustained and long-term across multiple life times.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think another part of what I find here is that I actually don't think different circumstances of Exaltation mean that much, as they're already done with when we enter play. </div> </div> </div>They mean a lot because the people to whom they've happened are people who are shaped by those experiences. However different two death knights might be, they were both at some point placed in the same position as they breathed their last breath and made the same choice. It gives a shared context to a splat right from the beginning. Not every splat needs it, but stuff like this can add some interesting nuance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Really I wonder why this element makes sense as coming before the Exaltation, rather than following the Exaltation? </div> </div> </div>Because this way leaves potential for some mortals who turned away from the call or who had it cut short, but were nonetheless touched by it. This likewise allows a chance to grow into one's power throughout the experience. With this approach, the journey <i>can</i> follow the receipt of the Exaltation, or the Exaltation can come right at the end, or somewhere along the way; whenever is appropriate. I see more value in leaving open the &quot;during&quot; and &quot;after&quot; options than strictly sticking to &quot;before.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Tidied up that last paragraph a smidge. 10-17-2014, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T11:53:51-07:00","id":285186,"title":"","content":"This is my new headcanon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T14:37:55-07:00","id":285421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/284076-alternative-lunar-exaltation-methods-lunars-and-the-call?p=285166#post285166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is an oversimplification. Different Exaltations work differently. Dragonblooded Exaltation isn't a choice, it's an inheritance. Liminal Exaltation is definitely not a choice: the new Liminal is a person who simply didn't exist before; it technically isn't even the choice of whomever accidentally created one. Alchemical Exaltation is a kind of choice, as you've framed it, but it is of necessity one that is sustained and long-term across multiple life times.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the Dragonblooded, depends on how much importance you place on Dragonblooded having to have a heroic element to their character to unlock it. I would say they have an element of choice (generally I think in life, heredity or genetic luck looms large for most qualities anyway).<br /> <br /> Sure, you're right that Liminals and Alchemicals have a broader perspective, although we don't really know what is the case with Liminals yet (perhaps there's a way their soul chooses life?) and I wouldn't call what the Alchemicals do choosing at all really. They are the weird guys though, to be honest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/284076-alternative-lunar-exaltation-methods-lunars-and-the-call?p=285166#post285166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They mean a lot because the people to whom they've happened are people who are shaped by those experiences. However different two death knights might be, they were both at some point placed in the same position as they breathed their last breath and made the same choice. It gives a shared context to a splat right from the beginning. Not every splat needs it, but stuff like this can add some interesting nuance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, I'm not saying they don't matter at all, just the pre-Exaltation journey has a relatively light bearing on what actually happens during the post-Exaltation life of the Exalt.<br /> <br /> If you take Sidereals, sure they're surrounded by destiny since their birth... but not much of their experience in play would seem to me to come from that itself, more from who they actually are, from what happens in play and after their Exaltation. They would be much less different if they weren't fated to Exalt from birth than if you changed virtually any characteristic about them. It's much less important - Exalts having unique Exaltation narratives actually seems of fairly minimal importance so most Exalts, with more bearing on the weird guys in particular (Alchemicals, Liminals), but even then, less than most other things about them (how they are beings who are created with their Exaltation from and by other humans).<br /> <br /> Which is why putting an emphasis on the journeys and landmarks as something in the Exaltation (if that's what would happen for Lunars, and it feels like it could make sense from the canon), rather than a precursor to Exaltation makes more sense to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/284076-alternative-lunar-exaltation-methods-lunars-and-the-call?p=285166#post285166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because this way leaves potential for some mortals who turned away from the call or who had it cut short, but were nonetheless touched by it. This likewise allows a chance to grow into one's power throughout the experience. With this approach, the journey <i>can</i> follow the receipt of the Exaltation, or the Exaltation can come right at the end, or somewhere along the way; whenever is appropriate. I see more value in leaving open the &quot;during&quot; and &quot;after&quot; options than strictly sticking to &quot;before.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, I can understand people being interested in &quot;almost Exalts&quot; of a sort I suppose (like the half-castes are). Re before or after, OK again but that is not the impression I got from the OP, which was that the Exaltation would always follow a journey narrative for Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T15:02:11-07:00","id":285440,"title":"","content":"I really like this idea. It is evocative, and it's easy enough to twist to fit almost any Exaltation story.<br /> <br /> Headcanon accepted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T17:28:39-07:00","id":285552,"title":"","content":"While I love the idea thrown out in this thread, I do want to put out there that I hope that this is NOT canon. I would love for the canon to stay normal, and to hear about one character who this happened to. This allows the possiblity, but doesn't force it onto every Lunar character constructed. Sometimes, that instant Exaltation fits a character story much better.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T08:41:55-07:00","id":285948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/284076-alternative-lunar-exaltation-methods-lunars-and-the-call?p=285552#post285552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I love the idea thrown out in this thread, I do want to put out there that I hope that this is NOT canon. I would love for the canon to stay normal, and to hear about one character who this happened to. This allows the possiblity, but doesn't force it onto every Lunar character constructed. Sometimes, that instant Exaltation fits a character story much better.</div> </div> </div> </div>It just would be nice if they were differentiated from Solars when Exalting, <i>somehow</i>, even if it's not in this particular way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T19:49:06-07:00","id":287131,"title":"","content":"This . . the thing about Lunars, that your post has made me realize about Lunar's and what they represent, is that they <i>Transgress</i>. They exist on the threshold (like those who gamble death, or <i>Desire </i>of the <i>Endless. </i>It's not a choice to become a Lunar, but it's still something you <i>become</i> rather than are. Argent Witches touched on it, but it all seemed a little too alien, this however makes so much sense. <br /> <br /> Yeah, this is a pretty fantastic idea that needs developing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T21:47:09-07:00","id":287250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/284076-alternative-lunar-exaltation-methods-lunars-and-the-call?p=285948#post285948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just would be nice if they were differentiated from Solars when Exalting, <i>somehow</i>, even if it's not in this particular way.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Personally, I would like to see the Lunars completely redone from the ground up. Everything overhauled. I want a new engine, new interior, new bells and whistles... in general I guess the chassis is ok. I like the way they look.<br /> <br /> I think that's what we're getting. So, yay?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T22:04:42-07:00","id":287255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/284076-alternative-lunar-exaltation-methods-lunars-and-the-call?p=287131#post287131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This . . the thing about Lunars, that your post has made me realize about Lunar's and what they represent, is that they <i>Transgress</i>. They exist on the threshold (like those who gamble death, or <i>Desire </i>of the <i>Endless. </i>It's not a choice to become a Lunar, but it's still something you <i>become</i> rather than are. Argent Witches touched on it, but it all seemed a little too alien, this however makes so much sense.<br /> <br /> Yeah, this is a pretty fantastic idea that needs developing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The only consistent theme I've seen about Lunars is that they change. They change their shape over the short term. They changed their Exaltations over the long term. They changed who they were. If you were to ask 10 Lunars what they do, you would get 10 different answers. And if you were to ask them again later, you would get 10 entirely new different answers. It kinda makes it hard to answer what the Lunars are all about, if the only thing they are is changing and adapting. Also, it's pretty reactive, rather than proactive, and I like my characters to be proactive. <br /> <br /> I like the idea of the Exaltation taking a while to really settle in on a Lunar, and some of that happening before the Lunar Exalts, and some of it after. I also like the idea that the Exaltation might decide to leave if the Lunar changes to become unfit for it. I like the idea that Lunars change everything. I just want someone who is more clever than me to integrate these themes with an aesthetic that I can understand, and make sure Lunars are as interesting in all regards as the other Exalted. That includes PCs, Elders, and the works. <br /> <br /> A Celtic aesthetic would actually work pretty well for them, I think. Celtic stories go beyond the summer of the story and into the winter of their characters. Modern day tales like the 'And they lived happily ever after.' In Celtic stories, that's the summer, and that's about the middle of the story. I think that works well for Lunars too. Here's an example:<br /> <br /> Celtic Hero:<br /> Spring: Hears seer say 'A child who picks up his weapons this day will die young, but be remembered forever.' Character picks up his weapons that day.<br /> Summer: Has fought many glorious battles, married, and is raising young children.<br /> Autumn: Children take up weapons and join the wars, just like their father, but too young. They are taken captive. Character picks up his weapons again, joins his old warband, and they go to rescue the children.<br /> Winter: The old warriors rescue the children, but many fall in battle, destroying their enemies. The hero is one of the last to fall, and he passes his weapons into the hands of his children, who fight their way to freedom.<br /> <br /> There's a lot more to Celtic stories, like a smaller scale (Lunars care for those close to them, or about nations, but not about concepts). Characters are often darker than elsewhere, but not less heroic: Revenge is a common theme, and is seen as honorable. Characters are reasonable, however: If an offense is given, they pay back what is due. Revenge only enters into it if the price is so steep the offender refuses to pay it or the offender is a real jerk and refuses to pay a reasonable price. And both sides will have supporters deciding the other guy is wrong. Same with duels, unless both sides really want to fight. That's ok then. And that is WAY better than Lunars and their debt-bond thing with silver tattooes. Very similar, but way better.<br /> <br /> Of course, the barbarian aesthetic sticks here too: To a Celt, if you had 25 men who followed you into battle, you were a king (or a chieftain, depending on how you want to translate the word). Also, arms and equipment were less important than your heroism.<br /> <br /> Oaths and geasa are awesome. That kind of became a Fair Folk thing, but Lunars should touch on it. I'd love to see that both sides claim the other side stole it from them. The four Celtic Geasa also are very appropriate for Lunars: Not sure if I can remember them all right now, but its something like Hospitality, honor, valour, and luck. I don't really want to go try to look these up, and I'm sure someone here can explain them much better than me (and correct me, because I know I'm wrong on those). That's WAY better than the Lunar thing of Obedience, Paranoia, Anger, Make a society.<br /> <br /> Lunars are not Werewolves. Give them something new. Please?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T03:58:57-07:00","id":287430,"title":"","content":"This is a brilliant idea and most assuredly in thematic harmony with the Lunars as they are presented. The offer of Exaltation is placed before the would-be hero, but they must survive a vision-quest and endure hardship and testing along the way. Very much in line with Lunar mindset. I also really like that the potential Lunar will meet possible allies/rivals and possibly a mentor along the way. This mimics the elements of the heroes journey as seen in many mythic traditions (which is what I'm sure the TC was going for).<br /> <br /> An element that I think could be included is that the Caste of the Lunar is decided by how the potential Lunar decides to circumvent the obstacles placed within her path. A Lunar who prefers a direct, physical approach would more than likely Exalt as a Full Moon. The Exalt who uses cunning would likely Exalt as a Changing moon, and those who use their intellect or wits would likely exalt as a No-moon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T06:53:11-07:00","id":287569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/284076-alternative-lunar-exaltation-methods-lunars-and-the-call?p=287250#post287250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I would like to see the Lunars completely redone from the ground up. Everything overhauled. I want a new engine, new interior, new bells and whistles... in general I guess the chassis is ok. I like the way they look.<br /> <br /> I think that's what we're getting. So, yay?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, I don't think we're getting <i>that </i>comprehensive a change. We're probably getting a lot of changes, but I think Lunars are going to be more recognizable compared to their past forms than than the combat or social systems are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T08:22:40-07:00","id":287654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/284076-alternative-lunar-exaltation-methods-lunars-and-the-call?p=287255#post287255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lunars are not Werewolves. Give them something new. Please?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In some capacities, they are not werewolves. Most of these happen to be of the &quot;monster existing to be slain in story&quot; and &quot;cannot control self&quot; type of feature. In other respects, especially of deviations from various stories that occur in W:TA or W:TF, <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=K88EqLQvYjQ\" target=\"_blank\">there's not much to separate them.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T09:18:48-07:00","id":287720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/284076-alternative-lunar-exaltation-methods-lunars-and-the-call?p=287654#post287654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In some capacities, they are not werewolves. Most of these happen to be of the &quot;monster existing to be slain in story&quot; and &quot;cannot control self&quot; type of feature. In other respects, especially of deviations from various stories that occur in W:TA or W:TF, <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=K88EqLQvYjQ\" target=\"_blank\">there's not much to separate them.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is mainly that a lot of conceits that work for Werewolf (particularly WtA, I have never had interest in WtF and don't follow it) just don't work for Lunars.<br /> <br /> The nature of strictly-hierarchical Garou tribal society, including its longstanding intranecine strife (Red Talons vs homids; Pure Landers vs Wyrmcomers; Shadow Lords vs Silver Fangs); the fight against an insidious, corrupting, objectively-evil entity which is actively working to make the world more terrible through many different pawns; the notion that every werewolf dead is a loss that can never be replaced, in the face of enemies who possess overwhelming numerical superiority; the theme that human progress and technological innovation are literally killing the natural world - these aren't really themes reflected in Exalted (well, except that DBs have the numbers advantage, but Lunars <i>do</i> come back).<br /> <br /> To my view, about all Werewolves and Lunars have in common is shapeshifting and the possession of magical powers, and even those are handed quite differently. I think of all the splats, Lunars have evolved the least from their WoD roots (Abyssals/Vampires; Sidereals/Mages; GSPs/Kindred of the East) and the lack of evolution has done them one hell of a thematic disservice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T15:11:29-07:00","id":287996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/284076-alternative-lunar-exaltation-methods-lunars-and-the-call?p=287569#post287569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is, I don't think we're getting <i>that </i>comprehensive a change. We're probably getting a lot of changes, but I think Lunars are going to be more recognizable compared to their past forms than than the combat or social systems are.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, I think they are. The devs (from what I understand) are going right back to the Lunar's roots, and saying what are these? What do they do? What stories do they tell? They will rebuild from there. Much of what they have now will be kept, but the foundation will be different. Right now, I feel that foundation is lacking. What does the Lunar Host do? The Silver Pact? Well, it doesn't let Lunars kill Lunars. And it encourages them to... train young Lunars, and stuff. Some movers and shakers build societies. What are Lunars all about? Whatever they choose. What did they choose? Some stuff. To each his own. It's a little... lacking in roots. I think it could be better.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T19:44:48-07:00","id":288168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ejtaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/284076-alternative-lunar-exaltation-methods-lunars-and-the-call?p=287996#post287996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I think they are. The devs (from what I understand) are going right back to the Lunar's roots, and saying what are these?</div> </div> </div> </div>To some extent, this is true. The <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:on-lunar-barbarism\" target=\"_blank\">titanic barbarian post</a> Holden made definitely indicates they're definitely putting in a lot of thought here (in case that was in doubt). However, I don't think Lunars are ultimately going to be as comprehensively dissimilar from what they are as you might think. Spoilering a quote from John for space:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It isn't as hard as people think it is to make Lunars good. They have all the ingredients for a great design. It's the presentation that has always been the problem. A good presentation breaks down biases and eliminates misconceptions about your ideas. This is one of the fundamental concepts of good design.<br /> <br /> People turn away from classic Lunars and change them into something else because they aren't good at design.<br /> <br /> It's not a habit I foster with anyone I work with. I push them to understand the reason why something failed, to get to the closest statement of a problem in order to supply the best solution.<br /> <br /> It all goes back to my first axiom: You can never produce the best solution until you make the truest statement about what the problem is.<br /> <br /> Over time, that has grown to encompass another statement: You may not find the best solution your first try, but the one you find will lead you to the one you need.<br /> <br /> I think that people don't understand what was wrong with Lunars, so they avoid the problem by just getting rid of whatever they can't explain.<br /> <br /> This has caused Lunar fans to ask me to remove the following things:<br /> <br /> -Tattoos<br /> -Tells<br /> -Shapeshifting<br /> -Shapeshifting into animals<br /> -Solar bond<br /> -Association with barbarians<br /> -Elder Lunars<br /> -The Silver Pact<br /> -The lost castes<br /> <br /> Given the tremendous ingredients above, when what you have left isn't identifiable as what you started out with, you're doing it wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> Naturally, the presentation on which they decide -- and, hell, what many of those things even <i>mean</i> in the new approach and context-- is hard to predict at this point. I just get the sense that Lunars are going to look both more different in some ways and more similar in others than most might expect. Or it may be some manner of optical illusion, where it looks mostly the same as what we've seen, but casting the right light on it causes something genuinely interesting and compelling to jump out. We shall see!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T21:21:44-07:00","id":288229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/284076-alternative-lunar-exaltation-methods-lunars-and-the-call?p=288168#post288168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To some extent, this is true. The <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:on-lunar-barbarism\" target=\"_blank\">titanic barbarian post</a> Holden made definitely indicates they're definitely putting in a lot of thought here (in case that was in doubt). However, I don't think Lunars are ultimately going to be as comprehensively dissimilar from what they are as you might think. Spoilering a quote from John for space:<br /> <br /> <br /> Naturally, the presentation on which they decide -- and, hell, what many of those things even <i>mean</i> in the new approach and context-- is hard to predict at this point. I just get the sense that Lunars are going to look both more different in some ways and more similar in others than most might expect. Or it may be some manner of optical illusion, where it looks mostly the same as what we've seen, but casting the right light on it causes something genuinely interesting and compelling to jump out. We shall see!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think you are either misunderstanding me, or I am not describing my opinion very well. Re-reading the above, I think the latter is the case.<br /> <br /> I love what Lunars are, and what they CAN do. I like their powers in general (though they could use some clean up). What I don't love, are the little things that form the (very flimsy and loose) foundation. Their foundation seems to be what they don't like and haven't killed yet. They hate the Realm, but haven't torn it down yet. They hate the Sidereals, but are too afraid of them to strike directly. Lunars hate Fair Folk but can't kill them all, because there are always more. Lunars hate and fear things... and love nothing. Oh, life and Creation in general, but not in the specific. They are bonded to their Solar mates, except that mostly they hate them. They love Luna. They love Gaia because Luna does, and so they do too. Sometimes they love each other. And that's it. Sometimes they do things, but they either do it out of anger, or to screw with you, or they are super clinical about it. Killing it when they are done with it, or ignoring it and leaving it alone. <br /> <br /> This has started to change, a little bit, in some of the most recent stories. But not much, because there hasn't been much published since the changes started.<br /> <br /> An entire line of characters focused exclusively on their darker emotions is... depressing and dull. Even the Abyssals have a great deal more love in them, even if it is twisted into something dark. Even the Infernals love themselves. Lunars are dripping in self-loathing. They don't even have what little the worst of the other lines have. A line of characters who have nothing they really care about occupies a space more appropriately reserved for NPCs. Villains, anti-heroes, obstacles, people to be redeemed... but in a game like Exalted, which is all about hope and building and human potential, Lunars don't share that.<br /> <br /> What do Lunars love? What do Lunars want to do? Can a Lunar exist who isn't based on feeling either hatred or nothing?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T22:14:35-07:00","id":288291,"title":"","content":"What do Solars love? What do Solars want to do? Can a Solar exist who isn't based on feeling either hatred or nothing?<br /> <br /> It's pretty easy for an entire group of individuals to hate a world-spanning empire that persecutes them without exception. Having the entire group love something - <i>any</i> one thing - across the board is a little harder to justify.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-21-2014, 01:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T22:53:38-07:00","id":288358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/284076-alternative-lunar-exaltation-methods-lunars-and-the-call?p=287720#post287720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is mainly that a lot of conceits that work for Werewolf (particularly WtA, I have never had interest in WtF and don't follow it) just don't work for Lunars.<br /> <br /> The nature of strictly-hierarchical Garou tribal society, including its longstanding intranecine strife (Red Talons vs homids; Pure Landers vs Wyrmcomers; Shadow Lords vs Silver Fangs); the fight against an insidious, corrupting, objectively-evil entity which is actively working to make the world more terrible through many different pawns; the notion that every werewolf dead is a loss that can never be replaced, in the face of enemies who possess overwhelming numerical superiority; the theme that human progress and technological innovation are literally killing the natural world - these aren't really themes reflected in Exalted (well, except that DBs have the numbers advantage, but Lunars <i>do</i> come back).<br /> <br /> To my view, about all Werewolves and Lunars have in common is shapeshifting and the possession of magical powers, and even those are handed quite differently. I think of all the splats, Lunars have evolved the least from their WoD roots (Abyssals/Vampires; Sidereals/Mages; GSPs/Kindred of the East) and the lack of evolution has done them one hell of a thematic disservice.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of the minute details of W:TA actually have anything to do with this. Take a few steps back, and you can see monsters that can opt to be more fighting a desperate struggle down to the bitter end. Which is a nice parallel with Lunars never giving up against the Realm, without being the exact same setup, since they have a far greater assurance that they can bleed the enemy down before gaining the advantage.<br /> <br /> And seriously, never assume that I'm suggesting that details from W:TA get ported over wholesale like the clumsy Renown system from 1e. That is a glaring bad faith assumption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T07:10:41-07:00","id":288507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/284076-alternative-lunar-exaltation-methods-lunars-and-the-call?p=288168#post288168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To some extent, this is true. The <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:on-lunar-barbarism\" target=\"_blank\">titanic barbarian post</a> Holden made definitely indicates they're definitely putting in a lot of thought here (in case that was in doubt). However, I don't think Lunars are ultimately going to be as comprehensively dissimilar from what they are as you might think. Spoilering a quote from John for space:<br /> <br /> Naturally, the presentation on which they decide -- and, hell, what many of those things even <i>mean</i> in the new approach and context-- is hard to predict at this point. I just get the sense that Lunars are going to look both more different in some ways and more similar in others than most might expect. Or it may be some manner of optical illusion, where it looks mostly the same as what we've seen, but casting the right light on it causes something genuinely interesting and compelling to jump out. We shall see!</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say the idea put forward in this thread counts as a radical overhaul, though. It adds, rather than taking away any of the Lunars' existing themes and elements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T07:28:11-07:00","id":288519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/284076-alternative-lunar-exaltation-methods-lunars-and-the-call?p=288358#post288358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And seriously, never assume that I'm suggesting that details from W:TA get ported over wholesale like the clumsy Renown system from 1e. That is a glaring bad faith assumption.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is it a bad faith assumption? A lot of that stuff was already ported from WoD to Exalted in 1e, and carried over into 2e, <i>and it's still crap</i>. I'm not suggesting you think things should be ported; they were ported 10 years ago, never left, and massively suck.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/284076-alternative-lunar-exaltation-methods-lunars-and-the-call?p=288168#post288168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Naturally, the presentation on which they decide -- and, hell, what many of those things even <i>mean</i> in the new approach and context-- is hard to predict at this point. I just get the sense that Lunars are going to look both more different in some ways and more similar in others than most might expect. Or it may be some manner of optical illusion, where it looks mostly the same as what we've seen, but casting the right light on it causes something genuinely interesting and compelling to jump out. We shall see!</div> </div> </div> </div>I generally don't agree with M\u00f8rke's take on this issue, nor the sort of attitude he fosters in that quoted post. I totally disagree with this notion:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that people don't understand what was wrong with Lunars, so they avoid the problem by just getting rid of whatever they can't explain . . . when what you have left isn't identifiable as what you started out with, you're doing it wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>People identify things that they see as being wrong or un-fun about Lunars. Whether or not that gets to the core of &quot;bad Lunar stuff&quot; is, in some ways, irrelevant. You can revamp the splat to have the coolest backstory possible and formlock will still be a shit mechanic to put on players, the baseline tattoo rules will still be an air-breathing mermaid XP tax to get around, the breaking of the castes still says something bad about the permanence of the Lunar Exaltation itself, etc. The Silver Pact will likely remain generally incomprehensible as A Thing That Exists because it was based off of WoD assumptions that don't hold true in the Exalted world.<br /> <br /> Just because something has been around forever doesn't mean it's worth keeping; if your largest concern is drawing players in, new or old, why the focus on keeping bad old stuff in when you can change it, save for nostalgia? If the original assumption was &quot;these guys will never get PC rules....oh shit give them PC rules hurry!&quot; then why hold on to conceits that were born from that initial frantic period and clearly were not well thought-out?<br /> <br /> The conservative approach didn't work with 2e. Ergo why not try out being revolutionary? Lunars deserve it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T08:00:18-07:00","id":288540,"title":"","content":"So, I'm stealing this and using it for my Creation...but, um, replacing the &quot;Lunars&quot; bits with The Chosen of Journeys instead. Because a gradual awakening to fated power after you answer the call and accept your heroic Destiny...that's some wonderful Sidereal fodder, right there. Complete with other Sidereals guiding you on your journey, many of whom you won't recognize as your guides until after your Exaltation.<br /> <br /> Still like my Lunar characters to be about Survival, Love, or transgressive states like madness or societally discouraged attitudes or beliefs. Luna doesn't choose people who answer a call and go on a transformative journey that turns them into someone new: she Exalts those who hold fast to themselves and to what's important to them in the face of an existential crisis. Such people are strong enough not to lose themselves once they are wearing different faces and wandering in alien worlds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T08:12:54-07:00","id":288544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/284076-alternative-lunar-exaltation-methods-lunars-and-the-call?p=288519#post288519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is it a bad faith assumption? A lot of that stuff was already ported from WoD to Exalted in 1e, and carried over into 2e, <i>and it's still crap</i>. I'm not suggesting you think things should be ported; they were ported 10 years ago, never left, and massively suck.</div> </div> </div> </div>You made a laundry list of random details from Apocalypse that obviously wouldn't fit. These are not necessary to tap into select themes of W:TA, and I think that you know that. There need not be a set of tribes to have monstrous heroes struggling against the odds for millennia. Once you've identified the differing conceits, porting over easter eggs and nods in a way that fits with Exalted becomes an easier task.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> People identify things that they see as being wrong or un-fun about Lunars. Whether or not that gets to the core of &quot;bad Lunar stuff&quot; is, in some ways, irrelevant. You can revamp the splat to have the coolest backstory possible and formlock will still be a shit mechanic to put on players, the baseline tattoo rules will still be an air-breathing mermaid XP tax to get around, the breaking of the castes still says something bad about the permanence of the Lunar Exaltation itself, etc. The Silver Pact will likely remain generally incomprehensible as A Thing That Exists because it was based off of WoD assumptions that don't hold true in the Exalted world. </div> </div> </div>The Pact is very far from being a WoD assumption thing. It's a group of Lunars with a loose arrangement to cooperate for the purposes of furthering a guerilla war against the Dragon-Blooded and Sidereals, and the territories that they control. You need a coordination system of some kind. Most of the parts of the Silver Way are there to facilitate this organization when they aren't reactions to the comprehensive attempts by Dragon-Blooded and Sidereal control to destroy them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just because something has been around forever doesn't mean it's worth keeping; if your largest concern is drawing players in, new or old, why the focus on keeping bad old stuff in when you can change it, save for nostalgia? If the original assumption was &quot;these guys will never get PC rules....oh shit give them PC rules hurry!&quot; then why hold on to conceits that were born from that initial frantic period and clearly were not well thought-out?<br /> <br /> The conservative approach didn't work with 2e. Ergo why not try out being revolutionary? Lunars deserve it. </div> </div> </div>The approach for 2e was to make everything crap compared to Solars, and tried to make nothing in the setting be worth saving. That kind of poisons things from the start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T09:16:21-07:00","id":288611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/284076-alternative-lunar-exaltation-methods-lunars-and-the-call?p=288507#post288507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't say the idea put forward in this thread counts as a radical overhaul, though. It adds, rather than taking away any of the Lunars' existing themes and elements.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mostly agree.* My post wasn't about Aquillion's idea, though: my post was very specifically addressed to a tangential point I thought Etjaka was making.<br /> <br /> * The 'mostly' owes entirely to a personal uncertainty about what Lunar themes actually <i>are</i> going to be in EX3. An uncertainty I've had for a very long time, now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T09:42:32-07:00","id":288635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/284076-alternative-lunar-exaltation-methods-lunars-and-the-call?p=288519#post288519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally don't agree with M\u00f8rke's take on this issue, nor the sort of attitude he fosters in that quoted post.</div> </div> </div> </div>It should probably be noted that it came up afterward that he was using &quot;presentation&quot; to mean something that's, well... frankly, a hell of a lot broader than I'd have ever found it reasonable to presume. He felt the mechanics were absolutely a huge part of presentation, for instance. In light of that, I feel it's saying a lot less than it initially sounds. Certainly assuming formlock as it was is back isn't a valid thing to do.<br /> <br /> Really, his claim seems to boil down to &quot;these broad ideas I've listed are things people have asked me to rip out wholesale, and I won't, because I see a way to rework them and put them together in a way that makes them compelling.&quot; As a possible example of the sort of &quot;keeping an idea, but changing its context enormously,&quot; there have been implications the Lost Castes stem in part or in their entirety from something the Lunars purposefully did to themselves, and that they are not displeased with the results. I think we'll really have to wait and see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T04:37:32-07:00","id":291953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/284076-alternative-lunar-exaltation-methods-lunars-and-the-call?p=288519#post288519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People identify things that they see as being wrong or un-fun about Lunars. Whether or not that gets to the core of &quot;bad Lunar stuff&quot; is, in some ways, irrelevant. You can revamp the splat to have the coolest backstory possible and formlock will still be a shit mechanic to put on players, the baseline tattoo rules will still be an air-breathing mermaid XP tax to get around, the breaking of the castes still says something bad about the permanence of the Lunar Exaltation itself, etc. The Silver Pact will likely remain generally incomprehensible as A Thing That Exists because it was based off of WoD assumptions that don't hold true in the Exalted world.<br /> <br /> Just because something has been around forever doesn't mean it's worth keeping; if your largest concern is drawing players in, new or old, why the focus on keeping bad old stuff in when you can change it, save for nostalgia? If the original assumption was &quot;these guys will never get PC rules....oh shit give them PC rules hurry!&quot; then why hold on to conceits that were born from that initial frantic period and clearly were not well thought-out?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I was in favor of changing those things myself rather than getting rid of them. IE, Make spirit totems more inclusive in themes beyond animals, the bonds include a choice and Sidereals, the tattoos are a prepackaged part of the Exaltation. Perhaps the breaking of the castes is rather something that happened when the Celestines were making the Exaltation. Everyone agreed on 5 except for little ol' Luna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}